{"name":"Cool Blue","hex":"#4984b8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cool","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a mildly low temperature.","Allowing or suggesting heat relief."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A moderate or refreshing state of cold; moderate temperature of the air between hot and cold; coolness.","A calm temperament."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cool"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cool Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Cool Blue is a 1989 American romantic comedy film directed by Mark Mullin and Richard Shepard, and stars Woody Harrelson, Hank Azaria, Ely Pouget and Sean Penn."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/66/Cool_Blue_poster.GIF?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cool_Blue","wikidata":"Q1123902"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikim